    "count_exemption_axis": null,
    "note": "Consumer-local admission gate. Each entry pins four things measured from a native archive blob - its declaration set, the set of constant-buffer registers its body reads, how many times it reads each, and how many float4 rows its immediate constant buffer declares - and the check passes only when the reconstruction compiled from that blob's own macro set agrees. The pinned values were measured from the game bytecode with fxc /nologo /dumpbin, never from this repo's output, and were not revised against it. The claim is exactly this: these 27 macro sets compile, and what they compile to declares the same ABI and performs the same static constant reads as the blob each came from. Nothing here is a claim about execution, about visual fidelity, or about instruction-stream identity - the full BRDF core is structurally reconstructed and its SHEX/DXBC is expected to differ. No shader in this family is created or used at runtime by this repo, and nothing here is a claim about any runtime other than the one the archive was taken from, so it is neither an OG nor an NG claim. Producer execution status is carried per entry and is 16 execution_failed and 11 execution_unproven, with zero PASS; execution proof stays with the producer oracle in the sibling fallout4-re. dcl_temps is excluded because it is register allocation, not ABI.",
    "evidence": "Denominator is fixed and closed: the AE 1.11.221 archive carries exactly 27 blobs with DIRECTIONAL + DIRSPLITS=3 + RGBSPEC + SHADOW + SPECULAR, and all 27 are admitted here, so admission is 27/27 of a set that cannot be widened by choosing a friendlier subset. Those 27 collapse to three declaration groups and the group is a function of the FILTER axis alone: none takes the raw t4/s4 tap, PCF1/PCF9/POISSON take the comparison t5/s5 tap, and PCSS/PCSSPOISSON take both. The read-set is finer and separates the other axes - AMBIENT adds cb2[6..8], and BLENDSPLIT drops the cb2[9] SplitDistances gate in favour of the two cross-fades, which is also what moves cb2[10] from 2 reads to 5. The read-count is exact on every entry in both the DIRSPLITS=2 and DIRSPLITS=3 families, so neither declares a count-exemption axis. The six DIRSPLITS=3 IGNOREROUGHNESS blobs each differ from their twin by exactly cb2[1] -2 and cb2[2] -1. These static pins cannot adjudicate the texture-derived AMBIENT exponent; numerical proof of the native fixed-square path belongs to the producer oracle and is not asserted by this ABI artifact. The immediate-constant-vector pin is 1000 on the eight POISSON and PCSSPOISSON rows and 0 on the other 19. The rejected list is 17 single-mutation cases, each otherwise a valid DIRSPLITS=3 macro set, so every guard is shown to fire for its own reason rather than incidentally. The compile_only list is the 21 cells of the 6 x AMBIENT x BLENDSPLIT x IGNOREROUGHNESS grid that the archive does not carry; they are compile-only legality checks with no native blob behind them and no ABI claim attached."
  },
